                <head>Chapter IV: February 9–16, 1932</head>
                <p>Japanese Talk of Demilitarizing Shanghai and Other Port Areas in China by Powers;
                    Further Chinese Protests Against Japanese Use of International Settlement for
                    Military Operations; Appeal by League Council for Early Peaceful Solution at
                    Shanghai, February 9; Consultations of Secretary Stimson Respecting Formal Reaffirmation of Nine-Power Treaty of
                    1922; Protests by Powers Against Military Flights Over International Settlement;
                    Chinese Request That Dispute Be Referred by League Council to League Assembly;
                    Appeal by 12 League Council Members to Japan Respecting Treaty Obligations,
                    February 16</p>





























































































































